# What the repository keeps: the code (bin, src, web, tools, test), the docs and
# their gallery (docs/gallery - the README shows it), the release notes, the
# MIT LICENSE, the
# package files, the deploy workflow (.github), the agent's notes (.agent) and
# its silent live preview (.claude/launch.json) - the owner chose to keep both.
# Everything below is made on a machine, or belongs to one, and is not kept.

# dependencies: npm install brings them back
node_modules/

# made by the tools: renders and their sound, the static site
out/
dist/
# a render written anywhere else with --out, or a sound file
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mkv
*.mp3
*.wav
*.ogg

# logs and caches
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.npm/
.cache/
coverage/
*.tmp
*.temp

# secrets, should one ever appear
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# one person's settings: the agent's local permissions, editors
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# what the operating system leaves behind
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
$RECYCLE.BIN/
